          "namedBy": "s2a systems' post of 2024-04-13, 'An initial, more detailed analysis of the images from April 7 showed nearly 60 objects around the CZ-6A upper stage (2024-058B/59344)', as quoted by SpaceNews on 2024-07-12 (https://spacenews.com/chinas-long-march-6a-rocket-appears-to-have-an-orbital-debris-problem/): a rocket body in LEO with some 60 objects, as ESA's row has it (6,000 kg, LEO, 60 asserted, 0 catalogued), launched on 26 March 2024 (GCAT)" },
