          "namedBy": "s2a systems' post of 2024-07-05, 'And the CZ-6A upper stage of the Tianhui-5 2 launch. Recorded today, 05.07.2024 at 20:01:37 UTC over Australia. As last time, the upper stage produces a lot of visually detectable debris.', as quoted by SpaceNews on 2024-07-12 (https://spacenews.com/chinas-long-march-6a-rocket-appears-to-have-an-orbital-debris-problem/), on the day of ESA's row; the stage is 2024-126D (60214), 'CZ-6A Y7 Stage 2', in GCAT's satellite catalogue, where 2024-126C is the TH-5 adapter" },
